  "metric_views": [
    {
      "view_name": "material_order_metrics",
      "source_table": "material_orders",
      "dimensions": [
        {
          "name": "order_date",
          "expr": "order_date"
        },
        {
          "name": "material_category",
          "expr": "material_category"
        },
        {
          "name": "supplier_name",
          "expr": "supplier_name"
        },
        {
          "name": "delivery_status",
          "expr": "delivery_status"
        },
        {
          "name": "quality_result",
          "expr": "quality_result"
        }
      ],
      "measures": [
        {
          "name": "total_material_orders",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)",
          "comment": "Total material orders placed"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_order_value_usd",
          "expr": "SUM(order_value_usd)",
          "comment": "Total procurement value in USD"
        },
        {
          "name": "avg_lead_time_days",
          "expr": "AVG(lead_time_days)",
          "comment": "Average supplier lead time in days"
        },
        {
          "name": "delayed_order_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN delivery_status = 'Delayed' THEN order_id END)",
          "comment": "Delayed material orders"
        },
        {
          "name": "rejected_order_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN quality_result = 'Reject' THEN order_id END)",
          "comment": "Orders rejected on quality inspection"
        },
        {
          "name": "unique_material_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT material_id)",
          "comment": "Number of distinct materials"
        },
        {
          "name": "max_order_quantity",
          "expr": "MAX(order_quantity)",
          "comment": "Maximum order quantity"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_order_quantity",
          "expr": "SUM(order_quantity)",
          "comment": "Total order quantity"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "view_name": "capacity_utilization_metrics",
      "source_table": "capacity_snapshots",
      "dimensions": [
        {
          "name": "snapshot_date",
          "expr": "snapshot_date"
        },
        {
          "name": "material_category",
          "expr": "material_category"
        },
        {
          "name": "fab_line",
          "expr": "fab_line"
        },
        {
          "name": "bottleneck_status",
          "expr": "bottleneck_status"
        }
      ],
      "measures": [
        {
          "name": "avg_utilization_pct",
          "expr": "AVG(utilization_pct)",
          "comment": "Average fab utilization percentage"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_available_starts",
          "expr": "SUM(available_wafer_starts)",
          "comment": "Total available wafer start slots"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_consumed_starts",
          "expr": "SUM(consumed_wafer_starts)",
          "comment": "Total consumed wafer start slots"
        },
        {
          "name": "critical_bottleneck_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN bottleneck_status = 'Critical' THEN snapshot_id END)",
          "comment": "Snapshots with Critical bottleneck"
        },
        {
          "name": "unique_material_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT material_id)",
          "comment": "Number of distinct materials"
        },
        {
          "name": "max_utilization_percent",
          "expr": "MAX(utilization_pct)",
          "comment": "Maximum utilization pct"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Supply Materials and Capacity Allocation for a semiconductor IDM running multiple fab lines and procuring 20 categories of materials (silicon wafers, photoresists, specialty gases, sputtering targets, EUV pellicles, packaging substrates). Stakeholders include Procurement (supplier reliability, spend), Industrial Engineering (capacity utilization, bottlenecks), and the COO (fab loading, allocation discipline). EUV-related consumables and advanced-node materials often have single-source supplier risk and 90+ day lead times.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Fab utilization = utilization_pct (capacity_snapshots); target 85–90%, >95% raises breakage risk\n- Wafer starts: available_wafer_starts (capacity), consumed_wafer_starts (load)\n- Lead time = lead_time_days; specialty materials often 60–120 days\n- Delayed orders = delivery_status = 'Delayed'\n- Reject = quality_result = 'Reject' (incoming inspection failure)\n- Delivery statuses present: Delivered, In Transit, Confirmed, Delayed, Cancelled\n- Quality results present: Pass, Conditional, Reject\n- Plan adherence = plan_adherence_pct; target 95%+\n- Procurement spend = procurement_spend_usd (allocation_monthly)\n- Bottleneck = bottleneck_status = 'Critical' (fab line capacity-constrained)\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - material_order_metrics (source: material_orders) — dims: order_date, material_category, supplier_name, delivery_status, quality_result; measures: total_material_orders, total_order_value_usd, avg_lead_time_days, delayed_order_count, rejected_order_count, unique_material_count, max_order_quantity, total_order_quantity.\n  - capacity_utilization_metrics (source: capacity_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, material_category, fab_line, bottleneck_status; measures: avg_utilization_pct, total_available_starts, total_consumed_starts, critical_bottleneck_count, unique_material_count, max_utilization_percent.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. material_id, material_name, fab_line, allocated_capacity_units, consumed_capacity_units, plan_adherence_pct, procurement_spend_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Rank suppliers by delayed order count in the trailing 12 months — which carry the most on-time risk?",
    "Show monthly fab utilization by fab line for the trailing 12 months — where are we above 95%?",
    "Which material categories have the longest average lead times — which are single-source risks?",
    "Top 10 materials by total procurement spend this quarter, and how does that compare to last quarter?",
    "How has critical bottleneck count trended monthly by fab line — which lines need capex?",
    "Which suppliers have the highest reject rate — where do we have quality exposure?",
    "What is the trailing 6-month plan adherence percentage by material category, and which categories are below the 95% target?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique total material orderss?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(total_material_orders) AS total_material_orders",
        "FROM {fqn}.material_order_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has unique materials changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(unique_material_count) AS unique_material_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.material_order_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does rejected order count vary across material categories?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT material_category, MEASURE(rejected_order_count) AS rejected_order_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.material_order_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY rejected_order_count DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the delayed order count by supplier name?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT supplier_name, MEASURE(delayed_order_count) AS delayed_order_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.material_order_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY delayed_order_count DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total quantity ordered (units vary by material) break down by material or component identifier for 'Delivered' records?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT material_id, COUNT(*) AS record_count, SUM(order_quantity) AS total_order_quantity",
        "FROM {fqn}.material_orders",
        "WHERE delivery_status = 'Delivered' GROUP BY material_id ORDER BY total_order_quantity DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total available wafer start slots for the week over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(available_wafer_starts) AS total_available_wafer_starts",
        "FROM {fqn}.capacity_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average percentage adherence to allocation plan changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT allocation_month, AVG(plan_adherence_pct) AS avg_plan_adherence_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.allocation_monthly",
        "GROUP BY allocation_month ORDER BY allocation_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sql_snippets": {
    "filters": [
      {
        "sql": "material_orders.delivery_status = 'Delayed'",
